      "questionText": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Complete the text, using the words given. You may make any changes to the words if necessary.</strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 75.4948px; border-color: #2dc26b; border-style: dashed;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"5\" cellpadding=\"5\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>outer space</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>ecological balance</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2872%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>fauna</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>orbit</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.4277%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>make up</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 33.2872%; height: 37.7474px; text-align: center;\"><strong>water body</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>Planet Earth is our home, and it is very special. When you look at Earth from <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.1</label><input id='fbo-907475-0' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='0' name='fbo-907475-0' type='text' size='13' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-0' /></span></strong>, you see a beautiful blue planet. This blue color comes from the many<strong> <span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.2</label><input id='fbo-907475-1' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='1' name='fbo-907475-1' type='text' size='13' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-1' /></span></strong>, like oceans, rivers, and lakes, that <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.3</label><input id='fbo-907475-2' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='2' name='fbo-907475-2' type='text' size='10' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-2' /></span></strong>&nbsp;most of Earth&#8217;s surface.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Earth is the only planet we know that supports life. It is home to a wide variety of flora and<strong> <span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.4</label><input id='fbo-907475-3' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='3' name='fbo-907475-3' type='text' size='9' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-3' /></span></strong>, including plants, animals, and insects. These living things depend on each other to maintain the <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.5</label><input id='fbo-907475-4' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='4' name='fbo-907475-4' type='text' size='19' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-4' /></span></strong>, which is essential for a healthy planet.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As Earth <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>15.6</label><input id='fbo-907475-5' class='ms fillblank-option-15' index='5' name='fbo-907475-5' type='text' size='9' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-907475-5' /></span></strong>&nbsp;the Sun, this creates day and night and the four seasons. This movement is essential in providing the right conditions for life to thrive, ensuring that Earth remains a habitable place for all living creatures.&nbsp;</p>",
